  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 round 2, item 9 + Q8">Scope: every surface this task touches. A record is selected for a person ONLY by one of these:
(a) `createdby` equal to the caller's systemuserid, when the caller is a HUMAN systemuser (`applicationid` null);
(b) a registry-listed CONTACT-typed "Assigned *" column (`MembershipOptions.CanonicalAccessConferringRegistry`) equal to the caller's linked contact;
(c) personal user ownership (`ownerid`/`owninguser` equal to the caller's systemuserid), pending escalation (a).
`owningteam`, `owningbusinessunit`, a team-valued `ownerid`, and every Team-, BusinessUnit-, Organization- or Account-typed descriptor select NOTHING on this surface. A team-owned record never fans out to team members.</constraint>
    <constraint source="#1044 split agreed with word-add-in-r1 (session27 Peer follow-through)">Scope: the createdby term. It binds only for a human caller. When the resolved systemuser is an application user, the createdby term binds nothing and a structured warning is logged. The BFF application user must never receive, through this surface, the set of everything it created.</constraint>
    <constraint source="#1044 split agreed with word-add-in-r1 (session27 Peer follow-through)">Scope: TodoGenerationService (all five rules), TaskActionCore, and the external-portal to-do create (`ExternalDataService.BuildTodoCreatePayload`). When the request or rule supplies no assignee, write `sprk_assignedto` (sprk_todo; on sprk_event for TaskActionCore) with the first of these that exists:
(1) the TRIGGERING person's contact: the playbook's acting user's linked contact for TaskActionCore; the calling contact for the external portal; the source event's assigned contact for TodoGenerationService rule 5;
(2) the regarding parent's responsible internal contact: `sprk_assignedtointernal`, then `sprk_assignedattorney1`.
If neither exists, leave the column blank and log a structured `todo_unassigned` warning. Never fall back to a team, and never to an email/name match. A supplied assignee is NEVER overwritten. Impersonated creates were rejected by the owner (they widen roles), so do not create as the user. The Office CreateTodoAsync is word-add-in-r1 task 083's; do not touch it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034 A1 / A1.1 (unchanged)">Scope: the authorization surface. Do NOT change what `AccessConferringOnly: true` returns or what `AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeForSystemUserAsync` composes. Platform ownership stays access-conferring there; the BU over-grant is C9 / task 036's work, not this task's. The new surface is a separate opt-in option. The default (`options: null`) AI-scoping behavior of `ResolveAsync` stays byte-identical for callers this task does not switch (`MembershipEndpoints`, AI scoping). The people option and `AccessConferringOnly: true` are mutually exclusive: requesting both is rejected with an ArgumentException, never silently merged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034 MUST (single mechanism)">Scope: the people-targeting surface. Implement it INSIDE `MembershipResolverService` as an option on `MembershipResolveOptions` (neighbor: `AccessConferringOnly`, `IMembershipResolverService.cs:197`). Do NOT add ad-hoc `createdby`/`owninguser` query conditions in the collector or BriefingService. That is the A1/D5 anti-pattern the ADR exists to prevent. The existing to-do/High Priority `owninguser` conditions (`DailyBriefingCollector.cs:1027`, `:502-505`) are REMOVED in favor of the resolver.</constraint>
    <constraint source="MembershipResolverService.HashOptions remarks (:1574-1601)">Scope: the new option. It MUST be added to `HashOptions` (`:1602-1616`). A cache key narrower than the query lets a people-targeted call and an AI-scoping call for the same user share one 5-minute entry, which is the exact disclosure task 043 fixed for `AccessConferringOnly`. A test pins that the two option values produce different cache keys.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6.5 + ADR-034 MUST (global field exclusions, .claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md:63)">Scope: `createdby`. ADR-034 requires excluding `createdby` as touch-history, and the owner's rule requires targeting it. Resolve by path B (see adr-tensions): amend ADR-034 (concise and full) with a "people-targeting surface" amendment that admits a HUMAN `createdby` on that surface ONLY. The global exclusion still holds for AI scoping and authorization. The executor drafts the amendment, and the MAIN SESSION applies it to `.claude/adr/`. The code MUST NOT merge until the owner approves the amendment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C7 / task 141 (owner Q3)">Scope: the Assigned-To term and the generators' contact lookups. Bind ONLY through `PersonIdentity.ContactId` as task 141 leaves it. NEVER fall back to matching an email, UPN or display name; that is the C7 hijack path. When the caller has no linked contact, the Assigned-To term binds nothing and a structured warning is logged, in the same shape as the existing `member_skipped` log at `MembershipResolverService.cs:894-900`. Created By and personal ownership still apply.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 fail closed + ADR-047 privacy invariant">Scope: every row returned by the Daily Briefing (render and email legs), the High Priority list and the Workspace top-priority matter.
- The final projection is read under the CALLER's Dataverse security, so Dataverse trims unreadable rows. Reuse `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` (MSCRMCallerID = caller systemuserid), or the delegated `IDataverseUserClient` where a user token exists. Do NOT declare a new impersonated-query interface.
- NO app-only fallback. If a channel's caller-context read fails, the channel is reported as FAILED in the collected payload (a marker distinguishable from zero rows), never as an app-only answer or a silent empty array.
- If every channel fails, throw, mirroring the OfficeService task-062 rule.
- Candidate-id lists are chunked so each impersonated request stays under Dataverse's URL limit. A failed chunk fails the channel; it never silently shrinks it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (discovered scope, no-deferral directive)">Scope: `CollectHighPriorityAsync`. It MUST stop returning flagged records org-wide. For each of the seven entity types, its result is the flagged records in the caller's people-targeted set, each readable by the caller. For `sprk_document`, which has no registry entry, the people-targeted set is the document's own person terms UNION documents whose `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project` is in the caller's people-targeted parent set. This matches the documents channel. `DailyBriefingSuggestionProducer` consumes the narrowed list unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the documents channel. A document is selected when its own person terms match OR its `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project` is in the caller's people-targeted matter/project set. The events channels keep the event-side OR regarding-parent structure (`DailyBriefingCollector.cs:754-768`), with every candidate set now people-targeted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 9 (binding)">Scope: LookupUserMembership. Add a `targeting` config key (`"people"` or omitted). EVERY live playbook in dev whose LookupUserMembership output reaches a CreateNotification, SendEmail or briefing node MUST be set to `"people"`; that is not optional. The node's default for non-notification consumers stays unchanged. The dev playbook edit is a configuration change recorded in notes, performed through the existing playbook deploy path (`scripts/Deploy-Playbook.ps1`) or the Dataverse MCP, never by hand-editing unrecorded rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034 (ours): event contract">Scope: the four publishers and `MembershipReconciliationJob.ReadLookupAsIdentity`.
- An event describes the row's ACTUAL owner after the write. Team-owned means `PersonIdType = Team, PersonId = teamid`. User-owned means `PersonIdType = User, PersonId = systemuserid`.
- Both writers (publisher and reconciliation) key the junction in the SAME identity space: Dataverse ids, not the AAD oid.
- The polymorphic owner is typed from `EntityReference.LogicalName`, never from `descriptor.IdentityType`.
- Both writers treat an application-user owner identically. Recommended: both skip it, because an application user is not a person. A divergence re-creates the key mismatch.
- Keep the wire contract's closed enums and property names. Do not bump `schemaVersion` unless the executor finds a consumer that parses the old semantics; in that case, escalate.
- Keep fire-and-forget (ADR-034 Q2).
- Do NOT add `createdby` events: the junction stores association, and the people-targeting surface resolves `createdby` live.
- Remove the false comments at `OfficeEndpoints.cs:1936-1941`, `DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:55` and `EventEndpoints.cs:393-394`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: `POST /api/v1/documents`. `TargetEntity` stays optional, because a document-only save with no related record is a required use case. Do not relax the alternate key on the SPE item id. Do not re-fix the owner/id hole (#1043); word-add-in-r1 owns it. Consume whatever owner the row actually has.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: #1044 coordination. word-add-in-r1 owns #1044 and PR #1045. Before editing `QueryTodosAsync`, check `origin/master` for their change. If they changed it, build on their version and reconcile it to the owner's rule rather than overwriting it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner (binding)">Scope: live verification. No Dataverse test in CI. Live behavior is proven by the MANUAL gate below, using the existing non-admin test users in the correct BU. Do NOT propose relocating users between BUs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner (binding)">Scope: this task's deliverable. No scope cuts and nothing deferred. Scope discovered during execution (another to-do writer, another consumer of the options hash, another notification playbook shape) is added to this task, not pushed to a follow-up.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR.
- State the placement decision: all changes extend existing BFF components. There is no new endpoint, service, interface, DI registration, package or Dataverse column; only the DailyBriefingCollector factory's constructor arguments change.
- Measure publish size against a FRESH master build from a short path with Compress-Archive. Report both sizes, the file counts and the delta. Ceiling: 60 MB.
- Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4">Scope: any Dataverse client touched. Do not add a new `.WithClientSecret(...)`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <adr-tensions>
    <tension adr="ADR-034" rule="MUST apply the 4 global field exclusions (createdby, modifiedby, createdonbehalfby, modifiedonbehalfby) — these are touch-history, not association (.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md:63)" path="B">
- Conflict: the owner (round 2 item 9, Q8) requires Created By to select a record for a person's briefing and notifications.
- Proposed path: B. Amend ADR-034 with a people-targeting surface that admits a HUMAN createdby there only; the exclusion stays for AI scoping and authorization.
- Path A (project exception) rejected: the briefing and notification surfaces are repo-wide and permanent, so every future reader would meet the contradiction.
- Path C (comply) rejected: no compliant shape expresses "the person who made it" once createdby is excluded. `createdonbehalfby` is also excluded, and it is empty for app-only creates.
- Numbering: take the next free amendment number at merge; 036 and 142 also amend ADR-034.
    </tension>
