  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Merge origin/master (with PR #1045) into this branch. Confirm task 141 has merged, and read how it exposes the linked contact. Re-verify every anchor in the background against current source; the collector and publishers are also touched by word-add-in-r1.</step>
    <step order="1">Draft the ADR-034 people-targeting amendment. It covers: the surface; human createdby admitted on it only; platform team/BU ownership and group-typed descriptors never select; event semantics are the real owner, in one identity space. Hand it to the main session for the `.claude/adr/` edit and owner approval, and apply the full-version edit in `docs/adr/`.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the people-targeting option to `MembershipResolveOptions` and implement it in `MembershipResolverService`:
- bind human createdby and user ownership to the caller's systemuserid;
- bind registry Contact-typed columns to the linked contact;
- drop everything else;
- reject the combination with AccessConferringOnly;
- add the option to `HashOptions`;
- log the no-linked-contact and application-user cases.</step>
    <step order="3">Switch `DailyBriefingCollector` (events, matters, projects, and the documents channel's parent and own-person sets) and `BriefingService.GetTopPriorityMatterAsync` to the option. Rewrite `QueryTodosAsync` and the High Priority to-do spec to use the resolver. Scope `CollectHighPriorityAsync` for all seven entity types to the people-targeted set, including invoice and work assignment, which have registry entries.</step>
    <step order="4">Route the final projection of every briefing channel, the High Priority list and the top-priority matter through the caller's Dataverse security, using the existing `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` or a delegated client. Chunk the id lists, add the failed-channel marker, and allow no app-only fallback. Update the collector factory in `AnalysisServicesModule.cs`.</step>
    <step order="5">Server to-do writers: TodoGenerationService (five rules), TaskActionCore (sprk_event.sprk_assignedto from the acting user's contact; plumb the acting user if the input lacks it), and the external-portal to-do create. Fill Assigned To per the constraint, never overwriting a supplied assignee.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the `targeting` config key to the LookupUserMembership node. Inventory the live dev playbooks whose LookupUserMembership output reaches a notification, email or briefing node (read-only query first). Switch each one to people targeting through the deploy path, re-query to prove none remain on the default, and record the inventory in the notes. Document the key in the node-author guides.</step>
    <step order="7">Fix event semantics:
- extend `MembershipChangedEvent` with a factory that builds an owner event from the written row's owner `EntityReference`;
- use the factory at the four publishers, reading the owner back where the create path does not already hold it;
- fix `ReadLookupAsIdentity` to type the polymorphic owner from `EntityReference.LogicalName`;
- apply the same application-user rule in both writers;
- remove the three false comments.</step>
    <step order="8">Write the tests listed in the acceptance criteria. Update `docs/architecture/membership-resolution-pattern.md` (third surface, consumers table), the collector's header comment (`DailyBriefingCollector.cs:16-31`, `:318-325`), and the `QueryTodosAsync` docstring (`:970-990`).</step>
    <step order="9">Build, run the unit suite and NetArchTest, then run the publish-size and CVE checks per §10.</step>
    <step order="10">Run the manual live gate and record the results (users, record ids, what each user saw) in `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-152-people-targeting.md`.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md, setting this task's status to `✅ [done]`. Comment on #1044 with the outcome for the membership half and the generator half.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Task 141's user-contact link is not merged, or does not surface the linked contact as `PersonIdentity.ContactId`. STOP. Do not substitute email/UPN matching, and do not accept coverage of only the 1-of-8 users who already have `sprk_primarycontact` as the finished state.</trigger>
    <trigger>(a) OPEN OWNER QUESTION: is personal user ownership (`owninguser` = caller) a person target alongside Created By and Assigned To? The owner named only those two. RECOMMENDATION: keep it. It names exactly one person, and dropping it would remove user-owned records that were reassigned to the caller in MDA and that the caller did not create. Proceed on the recommendation, but raise it in the PR and get confirmation before merge. If the owner declines, remove term (c).</trigger>
    <trigger>(b) OPEN OWNER QUESTION: High Priority scope. RECOMMENDATION: flagged records in the caller's people-targeted set that the caller can read, which is what this task implements. The alternative, "every flagged record the caller can read", would re-create a team/BU-wide list for broad-role users. Confirm before merge.</trigger>
    <trigger>(c) OPEN OWNER QUESTION: app-only creates lose the human creator (background item 8). Quick-create matters (Office) and POST /api/v1/events rows have createdby = the BFF application user, so under the owner's rule they reach their maker only if an Assigned column names the maker. RECOMMENDATION: events follow the agreed to-do rule (default `sprk_event.sprk_assignedto` to the acting user's contact when blank). Quick-create matters get NO automatic default here, because `sprk_assignedtointernal` on a root is grant-bearing under task 142. Record the gap and ask the owner whether quick-create should default an Assigned column (coordinate with 142 and word-add-in-r1). Do not silently add an owner-derived or createdonbehalfby term.</trigger>
    <trigger>(d) The external-portal "triggering person's contact" is the external contact itself. If task 142's Assigned-access materializer (or any Q5 auto-grant function) treats `sprk_todo.sprk_assignedto` as grant-bearing, defaulting it on external creates would issue grants. STOP and reconcile with 142 before merging that part.</trigger>
    <trigger>The owner declines the ADR-034 amendment or asks for path A instead. STOP before merge; the createdby term cannot ship silently against the ADR's global exclusion (CLAUDE.md §6.5).</trigger>
    <trigger>The impersonated or delegated read cannot serve a channel, for example because the environment lacks prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser on the BFF app user, the scheduled email leg cannot impersonate, or the seam cannot express the channel's filter. STOP and escalate; never keep the app-only read "for now".</trigger>
    <trigger>word-add-in-r1's #1044 change on master implements a different "for whom" rule from the owner's (human Created By plus `sprk_assignedto`). Surface the conflict; do not overwrite it in either direction.</trigger>
    <trigger>A live notification playbook turns out to INTEND team-wide notification (for example, a team-queue alert). That is a product decision against the owner's rule. Surface it rather than silently narrowing it or keeping it.</trigger>
    <trigger>A consumer of `MembershipChangedEvent` or of `sprk_userentityassociation` (topic subscription, junction reader, analytics) is found to rely on the old caller-oid semantics. Surface it before changing the wire meaning or bumping `schemaVersion`.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>
- Resolver option: its neighbor is `MembershipResolveOptions.AccessConferringOnly` (`IMembershipResolverService.cs:197`) with its filter `FilterToAccessConferringRoles` (`MembershipResolverService.cs:614-704`). Grepping `Services/Ai/Membership` for a "people"/"attention"/createdby-targeting option found none.
- Event factory: its neighbor is the `MembershipChangedEvent` record itself (`Events/MembershipChangedEvent.cs:68`), built inline at four sites today (`DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:63`, `EventEndpoints.cs:404`, `OfficeEndpoints.cs:1934`, `OfficeService.cs:942`) plus `MembershipReconciliationJob.cs:873`.
- Caller-context read: `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` (`Services/Communication/IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs:21`, singleton, unconditional at `CommunicationModule.cs:279`) is reused; `ExternalAccessModule.cs:187-193` already forbids a second such interface.
- To-do Assigned To: the column already exists (`MembershipOptions.cs:361-364`), and the Office writer sets it (`OfficeService.cs:2788-2791`).
- Nothing new is added: no service, interface, endpoint, DI registration, package or Dataverse column.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extend. The additions are:
- one optional parameter on the existing options record, plus one branch in the existing descriptor filter;
- one static factory on the existing event record;
- one constructor argument (an existing registered seam) on the collector;
- a column value at three existing create sites.
A separate "attention resolver" would be the second membership mechanism that ADR-034 forbids.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>
- Team-owned to-dos disappear from the briefing (#1044).
- Server-generated to-dos reach no one.
- Every user in a BU sees every team- or BU-owned matter, project and event in their briefing and in LookupUserMembership-driven notifications.
- Every user sees every flagged record in the tenant in High Priority, read app-only.
- The membership junction records a team-owned row as owned by whoever created it, under an identity the reconciliation job never matches.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

