  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. Resolver, positive and negative:
- With the people option, a record whose only link to the caller is `owningteam` (including a BU default team the caller is in) or `owningbusinessunit` is NOT returned.
- A record with a human `createdby` = the caller, user-valued `ownerid` = the caller, or a registry Contact-typed "Assigned *" column = the caller's linked contact IS returned.
- Team-, BusinessUnit-, Organization- and Account-typed descriptors emit zero conditions; the test asserts on the emitted FetchXML.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Resolver regression: with `options: null` and with `AccessConferringOnly: true`, the returned rows and the emitted FetchXML are unchanged from pre-task behavior. Existing tests stay green with no edits to their assertions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. Resolver cache: the people option changes the cache key. A people-targeted call and a default call for the same user and entity never share a cache entry (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. Resolver, no linked contact: a caller with NO linked contact gets Created By and personal-ownership matches only. The Assigned term binds nothing and a structured warning is logged. No email, UPN or name match is attempted; the test asserts the email path is not called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Resolver, application user: for an application-user caller (`applicationid` set), the createdby term emits no condition and a warning is logged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. Resolver, invalid combination: requesting the people option together with `AccessConferringOnly: true` throws an ArgumentException.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. Briefing to-dos: a team-owned open to-do due today appears for its human creator and for the user whose linked contact is in `sprk_assignedto`. It does NOT appear for another member of the owning team who is neither. The same holds for the High Priority to-do list. No `owninguser` condition remains in the collector's own query code (grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. Briefing entities: for matters, projects, events, documents and the Workspace top-priority matter, a team- or BU-owned record appears only for users it names (human Created By, Assigned, personal owner). A same-BU user it does not name gets nothing for it. A document the caller created on a parent that does not name the caller appears. A document created app-only on a parent naming no one appears for no one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. High Priority: a flagged record outside the caller's people-targeted set is not returned for any of the seven entity types.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Readability: a record in the caller's people-targeted set that Dataverse denies the caller is absent from every briefing channel, from High Priority and from the top-priority matter. The collector issues no app-only (`IGenericEntityService`) read for any row it returns. The test asserts zero projection reads on the app-only mock, and asserts that every projection read on the impersonated seam carries the caller's systemuserid.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Fail closed:
- When a channel's caller-context read (or any chunk of it) fails, that channel returns no app-only results and carries the failed-channel marker, which a test distinguishes from an empty channel.
- When every channel fails, the collector throws rather than returning an empty briefing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. Generators:
- Each of TodoGenerationService's five rules writes `sprk_assignedto` per the precedence rule.
- TaskActionCore writes `sprk_event.sprk_assignedto` = the acting user's linked contact when the input names no assignee.
- The external-portal create writes the calling contact.
- A supplied assignee is never overwritten.
- With no triggering person and no parent internal contact, the column stays blank and `todo_unassigned` is logged.
- No generator writes a team or matches by email.
- The Office CreateTodoAsync is unchanged by this task (diff check).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">13. LookupUserMembership:
- `targeting: "people"` passes the option through, and omitting it leaves node behavior unchanged (tests).
- The live dev inventory is recorded in the task notes: every playbook whose LookupUserMembership output reaches a notification, email or briefing node, and the change made to each.
- A re-query after the change shows zero such playbooks on the default.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">14. Events:
- For a team-owned row, each of the four publishers emits `PersonIdType = Team, PersonId = the owning team id, SourceField = "ownerid"`.
- For a user-owned row, the publisher emits `PersonIdType = User, PersonId = that systemuserid`.
- No publisher emits an AAD oid.
- An application-user owner is handled identically by the publisher and by reconciliation.
- Office save and quick-create gain publishing tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">15. Reconciliation:
- `ReadLookupAsIdentity` types a team-valued `ownerid` as Team and a user-valued one as User.
- The key it builds for a row equals the key the publisher builds for the same row (round-trip test).
- A pre-existing oid-keyed junction row for that row is returned by the orphan scan as a Removed event.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">16. Authorization untouched: `AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests`, and the `MembershipResolverServiceTests` for `AccessConferringOnly`, pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">17. Docs:
- The ADR-034 concise and full versions carry the people-targeting amendment under a number no other task has used.
- The owner's approval, and the answers to escalations (a), (b) and (c), are cited in the PR.
- `docs/architecture/membership-resolution-pattern.md` lists the third surface and its consumers.
- The node-author guides document `targeting`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">18. MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, existing non-admin test users in the correct BU, no user relocation):
(1) A to-do owned by the BU default team, created by user A in MDA, with `sprk_assignedto` = user B's linked contact, shows in A's and B's briefing and not in user C's (same BU, not named).
(2) A team-owned matter with B's contact as an assigned attorney shows for B and not for C.
(3) A flagged record naming nobody shows in no user's High Priority.
(4) A record naming B that B cannot open in MDA does not show in B's briefing.
(5) A TodoGenerationService to-do on a matter whose `sprk_assignedtointernal` is B's contact shows for B and not for C.
(6) A user with no linked contact still sees what they created and personally own, and nothing via Assigned.
(7) The scheduled email leg for B contains the same rows as B's rendered briefing.
Record the results in the notes with record ids.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">19. Build and supply chain: the BFF unit suite and NetArchTest are green. Publish size is reported against a fresh master build (both sizes, file counts, delta, zip tool) and is at most 60 MB. There is no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
