ESCALATION TRIGGERS: 141 link — not fired (branch carries it; ContactId surfaced). (a) personal ownership — kept [CORRECTED in verifier round 2: not pending — answered by owner round 3 B1, option (1)]. (b) High Priority scope — people-targeted set the caller can read [CORRECTED in verifier round 2: not pending — answered by round 2 item 9, raw/session27-owner-questions.json droppedAsAnswered "152(b)"]. (c) answered by S1 + A7, both implemented. (d) not fired (no grant path treats sprk_todo.sprk_assignedto as grant-bearing; reconcile if task 142's escalation (f) reverses). ADR approval — ADR-034 Amendment A3 (path B, numbering provisional; 036 holds "Amendment 2") applied to docs/adr; concise text in notes §8 for the main session [CORRECTED in verifier round 2: not pending — the owner approved path B in round 3 D1, "Path B for both"; only the main session's .claude/adr application remains]. Impersonation — not fired (the email leg is an authenticated request). #1044 conflict — not fired. Team-wide playbook intent — not fired (four live nodes, all per-user). Old event semantics consumer — not fired (MembershipJunctionUpdater writes PersonId verbatim; the other junction reader reads Contact rows).

PLACEMENT (CLAUDE.md §10, bff-extensions.md §A): every change extends an existing BFF component (resolver, collector, BriefingService, node executor, to-do/task writers, publishers, reconciliation). No new endpoint, package, option class, Dataverse column, interface, DI registration or plugin. TodoGenerationService registration changed AddHostedService -&gt; AddScheduledJob (ADR-036; ADR-052 §1 migrates a timer service when its behaviour changes; stays in the BFF: B2 uses BFF domain code TodoRegardingBuilder/CoreAncestorResolver, B3 daily low volume; now once per schedule across instances via the distributed lease). WorkloadPlacementGuardTests ratchet 14 -&gt; 13. No AI-internal type injected into CRUD code (ADR-013).

THREE-QUESTION JUSTIFICATIONS (CLAUDE.md §11), new internal static helpers, no DI:
- ApplicationUserCheck — existing: nothing reads systemuser.applicationid (grep); IdentityNormalizationService's PersonIdentity is cached and serialized on GET /api/users/me/memberships; extension: no, adding the flag there changes that endpoint's JSON and cache shape for one surface; cost: publishers and reconciliation decide "is this a person" separately (the oid-vs-id key mismatch this task fixes) and the resolver binds the BFF app user's Created By to everything it created.
- AssignedToDefaults — existing: Office CreateTodoAsync writes an assignee from its request only (word-add-in-r1's, untouched); no precedence rule exists; extension: one rule used by TodoGenerationService and TaskActionCore, inlining twice lets them diverge; cost: server-created to-dos/tasks name nobody and reach no one's briefing (#1044).
- MembershipOwnerEvents — existing: four publishers each built the event inline with the caller's AAD oid; extension: MembershipChangedEvent.ForRowOwner is the factory, this is the read-back + app-user rule around it shared by four sites; cost: four copies of the rule, the divergence that produced oid-vs-id keys.
Changed constructors (existing registrations, auto-wired): DailyBriefingCollector (IGenericEntityService -&gt; existing IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery), BriefingService (+IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery), CreateTaskNodeExecutor / ActionSeam / TaskActionCore / RecordCreationService (+existing IIdentityNormalizationService), EventEndpoints / DataverseDocumentsEndpoints / OfficeEndpoints handler parameters.

DISCOVERED DEFECT FIXED: BriefingService's top-matter detail query selected sprk_name, sprk_overdueeventcount, sprk_totalspend, sprk_duedate — none exist on sprk_matter (verified read-only) — so the top matter was always null. Now sprk_mattername / sprk_totalspendtodate / sprk_totalbudget, overdue Task events counted from sprk_event (due on or before yesterday), read as the caller.

STEP 9.5: code-review + adr-check over every changed file. Fixed: two XML doc blocks orphaned by inserted members (ExternalDataService BuildTodoCreatePayload's docs had attached to the new AssignedToBindKey const; EventEndpoints CreateEventInDataverseAsync's docs had attached to ResolveActingUserContactAsync). Accepted with reasons (notes §5.1/§6): TodoGeneration IntervalHours &gt; 24 now compiles to daily (cron), and non-divisors of 24 leave a short wrap gap — documented on BuildCronSchedule; Rules 1/3 target the event's responsible contact, not its sprk_assignedto (owner observation). ADR tensions: ADR-034 global createdby exclusion — PATH B (Amendment A3; approved by owner round 3 D1 — corrected in verifier round 2). ADR-052 — PATH C (migrated to IScheduledJob). Every new guard shown to bite: 30 seeded violations (resolver P1-P5, collector C1-C8, workspace W1-W3, reconciliation R1-R3, publisher O1/E1, defaults A1-A3, executor X1, external T1-T2, node L1, quick-create Q1, generator G1), each RED, sources restored and touched.

TESTS: full BFF unit suite 13,858 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (13,912); NetArchTest 341 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped; affected filters (BriefingService|DailyBriefing) 106 / 0. Client: Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components tsc --noEmit clean, failedSections.test.ts 5 / 0; the consuming src/solutions/DailyBriefing production build (npm run build) succeeded with 0 surface-owned tsc errors. No package changes (no CVE delta). Publish size NOT measured (instructed to skip).

PENDING MANUAL GATES (exact commands in notes §7): G1 deploy the BFF after merge approval; G2 switch the four live notification playbook nodes to targeting "people" (Deploy-Playbook.ps1 -DryRun then apply, or MCP update of sprk_playbooknode configjson for nodes 99f9ee9c…, b1d94997…, 4bd19f94…, e7b7e6a0…; re-query shows zero on the default); G3 task 141's gates (link coverage); G4 criterion 18 seven-case live gate with dev test users. Main session: apply notes §8 to .claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md (owner approval already given: round 3 D1; renumber if 142 lands first) and comment on #1044.
